# title: Shark fin note
# category: Barriers and touch options
# underlyings: 1
# source: Rubinstein & Reiner, Breaking Down the Barriers, Risk, 1991
# source: Bouzoubaa & Osseiran, Exotic Options and Hybrids: A Guide to Structuring, Pricing and Trading, Wiley, 2010
# summary: A capital-protected note paying 100% of the stock's rise, unless the stock ever closes at or above 125%: then only a 5% rebate on top of the capital.
#
# Notional 1000, capital protected at maturity. Up-and-out barrier 125%
# (daily closes), rebate 5% paid at maturity if knocked out.
# Its payoff chart looks like a shark's fin: rising, then a cliff.

2027-01-04
    s0 = spot()
    alive = 1

schedule(2027-01-05, 2027-12-30, 1D, US, F)
    if spot() >= 1.25 * s0 then alive = 0 endIf

2028-01-04
    if spot() >= 1.25 * s0 then alive = 0 endIf
    if alive = 1 then
        pays 1000 * (1 + max(spot() / s0 - 1, 0))
    else
        pays 1000 * 1.05
    endIf
